    "description": "As a Full Stack Developer at BFC, I design, architect, and deliver enterprise applications that automate complex business processes, optimize performance, and reduce operational costs across logistics, inventory, shipping, and order fulfillment.\n\nI translate business requirements and operational rules into scalable software solutions, owning the development lifecycle from system design and database architecture to implementation, testing, deployment, and continuous improvement.\n\nKey Responsibilities & Contributions\n\n• Design and develop full-stack enterprise applications using PHP, Laravel, MySQL, JavaScript, and modern web technologies.\n• Engineer automated workflows that eliminate repetitive tasks, reduce manual intervention, and accelerate high-volume operations.\n• Architect CSV/XLSX import and scheduled processing systems with dynamic mapping, validation, queues, retries, and notifications.\n• Build warehouse scanning and fulfillment applications with barcode validation, shipment tracking, and real-time workflows.\n• Integrate ERP, financial, inventory, and shipping platforms through RESTful APIs, including Fishbowl, QuickBooks, UPS, and USPS.\n• Optimize database queries, Redis caching, background jobs, and API performance to improve execution speed and scalability.\n• Modernize legacy systems and improve reliability through error handling, monitoring, and resilient processing.\nKey Achievements\n• Reduced bulk order processing time from 2 hours to ~15 minutes (87% faster) through caching and asynchronous processing.\n• Built reusable import and automation solutions supporting multiple enterprise clients.\n• Streamlined warehouse and fulfillment workflows through custom applications and automated business rules.\n• Modernized legacy integrations using RESTful APIs and OAuth 2.0.\nCore Technologies\n\nPHP | Laravel | MySQL | Redis | JavaScript | REST APIs | OAuth 2.0 | Queues | Bootstrap | Git",
